{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaqhobrBCavYqepyczcJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've proved `reverseAcc_fusion` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\nThe proof is an induction on `xs`, letting `acc` vary at each step:\n\n```lean\n  induction xs generalizing acc with\n  | nil => rfl\n  | cons x xs ih => exact ih (x :: acc)\n```\n\n- **`nil` case:** Both sides reduce to `reverseAcc ys acc` by definition, so `rfl` closes it.\n- **`cons` case:** Both sides unfold to the same statement for `xs` with accumulator `x :: acc`. That is exactly the induction hypothesis applied to `x :: acc`. This is why `acc` has to be generalized: the step needs the hypothesis for a different accumulator than the one it started with."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":7963,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491},"output_tokens":271,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9868cefd-0f80-4d18-8ff1-10ae1528d47c","uuid":"26592378-a0d4-417d-add5-b4556b176096","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:08:13.194Z","request_id":"req_011CgaqhoLybXsHrbD7GrUN3"}
